# Honeymoon 2026 — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the real values. Vite
# only exposes variables prefixed with `VITE_` to the browser
# bundle. Anything else stays server/build-side only.
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. NEVER commit a real key.
#
# This build is local-only (npm run dev) — there is no deploy
# configured, so there's no GitHub Actions secret to set up either.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# API key for Kai, the in-app AI trip guide. When set, the chat works
# immediately without asking the visitor to paste their own key.
#
# Get a free key at: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# Leave this blank to fall back to the user-supplied-key flow
# (each user pastes their own on first chat).

VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio narration scripts — out of scope for this build
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The template's pre-generated TTS pipeline (word-of-the-day and
# attraction narration audio) is not wired up for this trip. If you
# want to add it later, see scripts/fetch-attraction-audio.mjs and
# scripts/lib/*.mjs for the pattern, and set a server-side
# GEMINI_API_KEY (no VITE_ prefix) for those scripts only.
